## 2. The work
Implement exactly the PLAN steps named above, RED first (`heartbeat-worker` §2 refutation duty: property → mutant → RED → revert → GREEN → neighbouring mutant not caught; print `git status --porcelain` after every restore). Constants you TRANSCRIBE, never compute: (1) **THE CLICK RULE** (`PLAN.md:934-938`): one `onClick` on the privacy ROW; if the box is CHECKED → no `preventDefault`, and if the click did not originate on the input call `input.click()` so it unchecks through the path React listens to, then return; if UNCHECKED → `event.preventDefault()` unconditionally and open the modal in `mode="consent"`. (2) **THE PREDICATE READS THE MIRROR, NEVER THE DOM** (ticket `t_b7de5321`, ARCH-REV-S02 r3 N12, measured): jsdom and browsers set `.checked = true` by pre-activation BEFORE the row `onClick` runs, so `if (privacyInputRef.current.checked)` takes the CHECKED branch on a bare click on the EMPTY box and the modal never opens — the predicate is the React mirror (`privacyAccepted`, the state C4 shipped at `SignUpFlow.tsx:226-230`; the PLAN calls it `setPrivacyMirror` — transcribe with the shipped names). (3) **THE CANCELLED-CLICK RESYNC** (ticket `t_d9ccb5d3`, CODE-REV-S02-C3C4 r1 N1, BINDING, measured R0–R3): after `preventDefault()` React's value tracker desyncs and the NEXT genuine click fires NO `onChange`; remedy R1 — in the cancelling branch assign `privacyInputRef.current.checked = false` (a PLAIN instance assignment; R2 a synthesised `.click()` and R3 a prototype setter measured NOT to work), and the acknowledgement handler sets BOTH `privacyInputRef.current.checked = true` AND the mirror `true` explicitly (S02-S53 already says so). RED-first oracle: run `/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/dialectical-engine/.hermes/reports/consent-ui/probes/code-rev-s02-c3c4-r1-recovery.test.tsx` (copy it into your lane's `tests/render/` under a scratch name for the run, then delete it — it is the reviewer's kit, not yours to ship) and fold its property into `consent-signup-modal.test.tsx` as the mirror arm of S02-S52: after the uncheck route, `field("adult-affirmed").click()` inside `act` → `Create account` still `disabled`. (4) **C4's member-1 guard stays byte-identical** (`setPrivacyAccepted(event.currentTarget.checked && !event.nativeEvent.defaultPrevented)`); member 2 (the dismissal resync `setPrivacyAccepted(privacyInputRef.current?.checked ?? false)` on `onClose`) is defence in depth, shipped as the PLAN orders. (5) **FOCUS RETURN LANDS ON THE INPUT WHATEVER THE ENTRY POINT** (S02-S53/S54/S55/S56/S71): `useModalSurface` returns focus to the element focused at open — so the row handler focuses `privacyInputRef.current` BEFORE opening, or the text/control entry points return focus to `body`. (6) **V-16:** `Space` on the focused EMPTY box is a browser activation → the same click path (S02-S71 drives `.click()`; jsdom has no Space activation) — no keydown handler of your own; S02-S56's six-part Esc case is the B3 consumer half. (7) **V-18:** R17 cases 4 and 5 (`S02-S28`/`S02-S29`) reach "both boxes checked" ONLY through the acknowledgement route (`PLAN.md:1122-1133`); a bare click never ticks the box. (8) The modal renders OUTSIDE the `<form>` (S02-S57) in `mode="consent"` (S02-S58), consuming `PrivacyPolicyModal`'s four-member interface unchanged; `onAcknowledge` = tick DOM + mirror + close; `onClose` = member 2 + close. (9) `.consentPolicyLink` keeps `type="button"` and gains the SAME open route (S02-S51); the FIRST commit pins the attribute in `consent-signup-group.test.tsx`'s S02-S18 case (`getAttribute("type") === "button"`, RED against mutant m09 = attribute removed, GREEN at HEAD; never assert submit behaviour — jsdom cannot submit from a button activation). (10) `disabled={busy || sent || !adultAffirmed || !privacyAccepted}` (`SignUpFlow.tsx:243`) unchanged; request shape unchanged (R19); banned substrings (R21, `v2ui-node-runner`). (11) After the first commit re-run the C3 row's command ×3: its TEST count rises by one, its file count `<n>` does not (COMMON D4 wording). Colours only via `var(--token)`; new tokens go inside the two existing token blocks AND into `tests/unit/t9-mode-tokens.test.ts`'s maps (comma-tight). Gates before handoff, in order: (1) `pnpm run generate:contract` — say you ran it and that the tree stayed clean; (2) `pnpm typecheck` — report the DELTA against BASELINE.md (no diagnostic outside the 8 pinned in `tests/unit/s14-ui.test.ts`); (3) `pnpm exec vitest run tests/unit/t9-mode-tokens.test.ts` — the colour-literal hit list is exactly the one pinned line and the other six tests are green; (4) `pnpm exec vitest run tests/render/auth-flow-integration.test.tsx` — 17+ passed, or the SPEC-named updates with their reason; (5) your cluster commands ×3 (table: run 1/2/3, worst). Commit on `slice/consent-s02` ONLY when all owned clusters are GREEN on the worst run, message ``test(consent-ui S02-C3): pin type="button" on the Privacy Policy control` (first, ticket `t_155968da`) then `feat(consent-ui S02-C7): privacy row opens the policy; acknowledgement ticks the box` (one commit per cluster; the follow-up first)`; one commit per cluster is fine; never amend a reviewed commit. Write as you go (COMMON §4b).

