## Orchestrator addition — rulings from CODE-REV-S02-C5C6 r1 that BIND C7 (DECISIONS.md, 2026-09-07)
- **N7 — the modal is mounted CONDITIONALLY** (`{policyOpen && <PrivacyPolicyModal open mode="consent" onClose={…} onAcknowledge={…} />}`), so every open is a fresh read: the scroll gate resets, the reader starts at the top, `I have read it` is disabled again until the end. Pin it with ONE extra case in `consent-signup-modal.test.tsx`: open → drive the gate to the end (the acknowledgement route's metrics, without clicking `I have read it`) → close with `×` → reopen → `I have read it` is `disabled` again. A persistently mounted modal (state surviving the close) is the mutant this case catches.
- **N1/V-20 (S01's constraint, not yours, stated so you do not "fix" it):** the Esc stack resolves unrelated siblings by document order; in the sign-up card the modal is the only surface, so S02-S56 needs no arrangement — do not touch `modalSemantics.ts` beyond commit 2's comment lines.
- **N3:** `.policyGateHint` prints as visible footer text until C8 clips it — expected; never style or hide it from the component.
